1. Finding 1 is closed.
Python and TS seed the same persisted shape as Rust and production: `name, roles, fts_tokenizer, vector_embedder, vector_declared`, matching `persist_projection_row` in [lib.rs](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:17084). Rust uses `("status", "filterable", Some(""), NULL, true)` at [slice23_spec_validation_reject.rs](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/tests/slice23_spec_validation_reject.rs:142) and [line 429](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/tests/slice23_spec_validation_reject.rs:429). Python and TS use the same values at [test_slice15d_projection_registry.py](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/python/tests/test_slice15d_projection_registry.py:123) and [slice15d-projection-registry.test.ts](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/ts/tests/slice15d-projection-registry.test.ts:109).

The three oracles are present in both bindings: verbatim readback, re-apply raises `WriteValidationError`, adding `searchable` remedies it. Python: [lines 568-587](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/python/tests/test_slice15d_projection_registry.py:568). TS: [lines 701-728](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/ts/tests/slice15d-projection-registry.test.ts:701). They are actually a little stronger than Rust after the remedy, because Rust only asserts configure succeeds at [slice23_spec_validation_reject.rs:453](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-23-sv/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/tests/slice23_spec_validation_reject.rs:453), while Python/TS also read back the repaired row.

